    {
      "id": "ac286645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Articulation Agreement Overview This agreement outlines lower-division course requirements specific to the major. Students are strongly encouraged to consult an academic advisor to ensure they meet all degree requirements for their intended baccalaureate program. Helpful Resources: CSUB Catalog Transfer Admission Requirements Academic Advising Student Centers CSUB Program Pathways Mapper Course Equivalency Information for 4-Year Institutions Students and staff can explore course transfer equivalencies through the Transfer Evaluation System (TES) . Equivalency agreements are updated regularly and subject to change. For the most current information, please refer to TES or contact the Articulation Office .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>Articulation Agreement Overview</strong></p><p>This agreement outlines lower-division course requirements specific to the major. Students are strongly encouraged to consult an academic advisor to ensure they meet all degree requirements for their intended baccalaureate program.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Helpful Resources:</strong></p><ul><li><a href=\"https://catalog.csub.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSUB Catalog</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/admissions/transfer\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Admission Requirements</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/advising\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Academic Advising Student Centers</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/ppm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSUB Program Pathways Mapper</a></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Course Equivalency Information for 4-Year Institutions</strong></p><p>Students and staff can explore course transfer equivalencies through the <a href=\"https://tes.collegesource.com/publicview/TES_publicview01.aspx?rid=7ea49506-39bf-4815-8199-734369e7a30c&amp;aid=ccc830a2-2435-4dd6-b352-a586b4575654\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer Evaluation System (TES)</a>. Equivalency agreements are updated regularly and subject to change. For the most current information, please refer to TES or contact the <a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/articulation/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Articulation Office</a>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "ae286645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About the Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "b0286645-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Communications: To develop within students the technical skills, conceptual engagement, and critical courage necessary to explore the problems, processes, and potential impact of visual art, art history, and art education. Critical Thinking: To provide students with visual literacy and critical thinking ability to understand human experience and how the arts are uniquely equipped to impact it. Flexibility of engagement: To allow students multiple points of entry into the arts as art educators, art historians, and studio artists, and to be aware of the career options available to them both inside and outside of the art world. Personal development: To instill within students self-understanding, theoretical openness, social awareness, historical consciousness, creative confidence, and an enduring sense of curiosity. Career Opportunities A Bachelor of Arts degree from the Department of Art and Art History serves as a lens for understanding the larger world, offering students life-enriching critical thinking and problem-solving skills that will serve them well in any future pursuit. Our program provides excellent preparation for continued graduate study in fine arts and also offers a gateway into careers such as being an artist, art historian, researcher, art educator, curator, gallerist, or museum professional. For additional information, visit the following: Department of Art and Art History Program Requirements - Art, BA, emphasis in Studio Art",
      "contentHtml": "<p>Communications: To develop within students the technical skills, conceptual engagement, and critical courage necessary to explore the problems, processes, and potential impact of visual art, art history, and art education.</p><p>Critical Thinking: To provide students with visual literacy and critical thinking ability to understand human experience and how the arts are uniquely equipped to impact it.</p><p>Flexibility of engagement: To allow students multiple points of entry into the arts as art educators, art historians, and studio artists, and to be aware of the career options available to them both inside and outside of the art world.</p><p>Personal development: To instill within students self-understanding, theoretical openness, social awareness, historical consciousness, creative confidence, and an enduring sense of curiosity.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Career Opportunities</strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">A Bachelor of Arts&nbsp;degree&nbsp;from the Department of Art and Art History serves as a lens for understanding the larger world, offering students life-enriching critical thinking and problem-solving skills that will serve them well in any future pursuit. Our program provides excellent preparation for continued graduate study in fine arts and also offers a gateway into careers such as being an artist, art historian, researcher, art educator, curator, gallerist, or museum professional.</span></p><p><br></p><p>For additional information, visit the following:</p><p><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/art/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Department of Art and Art History</a></p><p>Program Requirements - <a href=\"https://catalog.csub.edu/academic-degrees-programs/undergraduate-majors/art-ba-emphasis-studio-art/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Art, BA, emphasis in Studio Art</a></p>"
    }
  ],
